---
title: Olive Garden Chicken Gnocchi Soup
description: Creamy copycat Olive Garden chicken and gnocchi soup with spinach and carrots.
source: https://tornadoughalli.com/olive-garden-chicken-gnocchi-soup/
author: Tornadough Alli
servings: 6
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
time required: 30 minutes
course: soup
cuisine: American
tags:
  - chicken
  - gnocchi
  - soup
  - olive garden
  - copycat
  - scaling
---

In a #large Dutch oven{} or stock pot, melt @butter{4%tbsp} and @olive oil{1%tbsp} together over medium heat.

Add @onion{1%small}(chopped), @carrots{1%cup}(shredded), optional @celery{1%cup}(chopped), and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). Cook over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until the onions are translucent, about ~{5%minutes}.

Whisk in @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} and cook over medium heat for ~{1%minute}. Slowly stir in @chicken broth{6%cups} and simmer over medium heat until the broth starts to thicken, about ~{5%minutes}.

Meanwhile, cook @mini potato gnocchi{16%oz}(1 package) in a separate pot of boiling salted water according to package directions until tender, or add directly to the soup in the next step. Drain if cooked separately and set aside.

Add @milk{2%cups} to the soup and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Stir in @parsley flakes{2%tsp}, and season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Reduce heat to medium-low. Add the gnocchi, @fresh spinach{1%cup}(chopped), and @boneless skinless chicken thighs{1%lb}(cooked and shredded). Simmer until heated through and the soup has thickened to your liking, about ~{5%minutes}. For a thicker soup, stir in 1 tbsp cornstarch mixed with 1 tbsp cold water.
